# Flowise VM — COMPOSE-LEVEL env. Copy to .env and fill in. The real .env is
# gitignored and written by the Ubuntu autoinstall (it sets ONLY PANEL_PASSWORD;
# PANEL_DOMAIN is left blank to auto-derive). NEVER commit a real .env.
#
# firstboot.sh AUTO-GENERATES the per-VM Flowise secrets into this file on first boot
# (FLOWISE_SECRETKEY_OVERWRITE, JWT_AUTH_TOKEN_SECRET, JWT_REFRESH_TOKEN_SECRET,
# TOKEN_HASH_SECRET, EXPRESS_SESSION_SECRET) — you do NOT set them here.

# === CloudHosting setup panel + TLS ===
# Panel login password. REQUIRED — the panel fails closed (PANEL_REQUIRE_AUTH=1) if empty.
PANEL_PASSWORD=REPLACE_ME
# Public host (TLS via Let's Encrypt). Blank => firstboot derives vps-<o3>-<o4>.cloudhosting.lv
# from the primary IPv4. Panel on :8443, Flowise UI on :443 of this host.
PANEL_DOMAIN=

# === Optional ===
# AVOTS_API_KEY only drives the panel's "connected" indicator (builder stub); the
# actual avots provider/key is configured INSIDE Flowise's own UI. Leave blank otherwise.
# AVOTS_API_KEY=av_mcp_...

# Flowise is a BUILDER: pick your LLM provider + paste your key INSIDE Flowise
# (open it from the panel's "Open Flowise" button). Nothing else goes here.
